  m_text: 'The sun beat down, turning the trail to dust as I rode my horse, Old Hake,
    into small town named rise. Sheriff Brody, a grizzled man with eyes that had
    seen too many sunsets, laid it out. "Got a job for you, cowboy. Big reward, biggest
    this town''s ever seen. There''s talk of some strange goings-on in Shadow Canyon,
    whispers of a forgotten gold strike, but nobody''s come back right from there.
    Just need you to scout it out, see what''s what. Be careful, though. They say...
    things ain''t right in there."



    The promise of riches was enough. I rode
    towards the jagged opening of Shadow Canyon, its walls rising like ancient giants,
    casting long, eerie shadows. I hitched Hake and stepped inside, the air instantly
    growing still and unnaturally quiet. The reward would be worth it, I thought,
    pushing deeper into the echoing expanse. '
